# MediaMTX — purpose & near-term focus (Orlando)

Colleague note: sync on purpose; he will be in **Orlando in ~2 weeks** for more testing. Until then **focus on infra**, not new features or CSI/MediaMTX merging.

CSI sensing and MediaMTX stay **separate** until we explicitly join them.

## Agreed purpose (lab)

```
Lab sensors/cameras (ESP32 MJPEG today)
  → one MediaMTX host (ffmpeg on that same machine if needed)
  → colleague consumes RTSP (path cam_xiao)
```

Same idea as Care.AI-style diagram: **local nodes in**, colleague is **RTSP client / AI**.

- ESP outputs **MJPEG HTTP** (`:81/stream`) — not RTSP yet → ffmpeg still needed
- **ffmpeg + MediaMTX on the same host** (Mac Mini preferred)
- Sensors must **not** hop through a third laptop; one media-server box only
- Colleague tap-in: `rtsp://<HOST_IP>:8554/cam_xiao` (HLS `:8888` backup; avoid `:8889` WebRTC over LAN IP for now)

## Infra checklist until Orlando

1. Single host (prefer **Mac Mini**) = MediaMTX + `publish_xiao.sh`
2. LabPSK reachability (client isolation blocks Mac↔ESP on some clients — use host that can `curl` the ESP)
3. Stable documented URLs / IPs + architecture diagram (`mediamtx/esp32-mediamtx-architecture.png`)
4. Keep stream up (tmux / auto-restart); Mac awake
5. Short runbook for colleague tap-in

## Do not prioritize until Orlando

- CSI GUI / calibration tuning as the main track
- Spectrum / SaiPhone / Guest Wi-Fi workarounds as the primary path
- Multi-laptop publish hops (Guest laptop as MediaMTX host)
- Hospital VLANs / TLS / GCP / recording (still out of scope)
- **MediaMTX A/V** (ESP mic PCM/AAC muxed with video) — parked; see `csi-detection-parked.mdc`. Stage 2 stays video-only until we explicitly pick this up.

